WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.246
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:08.862
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.162 --> 00:00:14.671
Unit ten: Digital Citizenship. Today you will give rules for online behaviour with 'must' and 'should'.

4
00:00:14.971 --> 00:00:17.797
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:22.442
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:24.377
Online etiquette.

7
00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:28.242
Online etiquette means polite behaviour on the internet.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.674
Good online etiquette means no shouting in capitals.

9
00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:35.087
Your turn. Say: Online etiquette.

10
00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:39.260
Online etiquette.

11
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:41.308
Digital rights.

12
00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:45.048
Digital rights means your rights when you use technology.

13
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.742
Privacy is one of our digital rights.

14
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.037
Your turn. Say: Digital rights.

15
00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.029
Digital rights.

16
00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:57.249
Responsible sharing.

17
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:01.538
Responsible sharing means thinking before you post or forward.

18
00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.800
Responsible sharing stops fake news.

19
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:08.547
Your turn. Say: Responsible sharing.

20
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.040
Responsible sharing.

21
00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:15.098
Cyber ethics.

22
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:18.896
Cyber ethics means right and wrong behaviour online.

23
00:01:19.483 --> 00:01:22.342
Cyber ethics says: don't hack others.

24
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.672
Your turn. Say: Cyber ethics.

25
00:01:28.533 --> 00:01:29.999
Cyber ethics.

26
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.390
Information literacy.

27
00:01:33.383 --> 00:01:37.415
Information literacy means the skill of finding and judging information.

28
00:01:38.017 --> 00:01:40.933
Information literacy helps you spot lies.

29
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:44.481
Your turn. Say: Information literacy.

30
00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:49.043
Information literacy.

31
00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:51.051
Digital divide.

32
00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:56.081
Digital divide means the gap between people with and without technology.

33
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.275
Free Wi-Fi can close the digital divide.

34
00:01:59.883 --> 00:02:02.838
Your turn. Say: Digital divide.

35
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:06.829
Digital divide.

36
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:08.817
Online community.

37
00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:13.291
Online community means a group of people who meet on the internet.

38
00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:16.661
I joined an online community of young coders.

39
00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.518
Your turn. Say: Online community.

40
00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:24.983
Online community.

41
00:02:25.717 --> 00:02:27.194
Constructive dialogue.

42
00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:31.785
Constructive dialogue means helpful, respectful conversation.

43
00:02:32.383 --> 00:02:34.859
Comments should start constructive dialogue.

44
00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.648
Your turn. Say: Constructive dialogue.

45
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.105
Constructive dialogue.

46
00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:45.606
Accountability online.

47
00:02:46.617 --> 00:02:50.288
Accountability online means being responsible for what you post.

48
00:02:50.883 --> 00:02:53.742
Accountability online means owning your words.

49
00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:57.490
Your turn. Say: Accountability online.

50
00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:02.182
Accountability online.

51
00:03:02.917 --> 00:03:04.440
Privacy awareness.

52
00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.214
Privacy awareness means knowing how to protect personal information.

53
00:03:09.817 --> 00:03:12.281
Privacy awareness keeps your data safe.

54
00:03:12.883 --> 00:03:16.012
Your turn. Say: Privacy awareness.

55
00:03:18.867 --> 00:03:20.495
Privacy awareness.

56
00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:22.924
Tech responsibility.

57
00:03:23.917 --> 00:03:27.658
Tech responsibility means using technology in a careful, fair way.

58
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:31.770
Tech responsibility includes screen-time limits.

59
00:03:32.383 --> 00:03:35.709
Your turn. Say: Tech responsibility.

60
00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:40.276
Tech responsibility.

61
00:03:41.017 --> 00:03:42.680
Inclusive space.

62
00:03:43.683 --> 00:03:47.111
Inclusive space means a place where everyone feels welcome.

63
00:03:47.717 --> 00:03:50.285
Our class chat is an inclusive space.

64
00:03:50.883 --> 00:03:53.919
Your turn. Say: Inclusive space.

65
00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.209
Inclusive space.

66
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.662
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:04:03.517 --> 00:04:06.747
Visal, what are the rules for being a good digital citizen?

68
00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:12.673
You must respect others online. You should verify before sharing.

69
00:04:13.783 --> 00:04:15.678
What about personal information?

70
00:04:16.783 --> 00:04:21.154
You mustn't share passwords. You should check your privacy settings.

71
00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:24.041
And if someone is unkind?

72
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:29.553
You should report it and keep the chat an inclusive space.

73
00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.328
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:33.183 --> 00:04:37.342
Grammar focus: Modal verbs (must and should) for online conduct.

75
00:04:37.642 --> 00:04:38.748
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.391
You must respect others online.

77
00:04:42.283 --> 00:04:44.294
You should verify before sharing.

78
00:04:45.183 --> 00:04:48.274
We mustn't post other people's photos without asking.

79
00:04:49.233 --> 00:04:54.106
'Must' is a strong rule. 'Should' is advice. 'Mustn't' means it is not allowed.

80
00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.907
Be careful! Don't say: You must to respect others online.

81
00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:03.946
Say: You must respect others online.

82
00:05:04.246 --> 00:05:06.954
After 'must' and 'should', use the base verb.

83
00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:10.431
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:11.233 --> 00:05:12.827
Good Citizens Online.

85
00:05:13.127 --> 00:05:16.171
Digital citizenship is about tech responsibility.

86
00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:20.548
You must follow online etiquette and respect digital rights.

87
00:05:21.533 --> 00:05:25.251
You should practise responsible sharing and information literacy.

88
00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.882
Privacy awareness protects you and your friends.

89
00:05:29.867 --> 00:05:33.666
Together, we can make every online community an inclusive space.

90
00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:38.803
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.406
You must blank others online.

92
00:05:41.706 --> 00:05:46.718
A, respect. B, to respect. C, respecting.

93
00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:52.452
The answer is A: respect.

94
00:05:53.617 --> 00:05:56.441
Polite behaviour on the internet is online blank.

95
00:05:56.741 --> 00:06:00.208
A, etiquette. B, divide. C, privacy.

96
00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.662
The answer is A: etiquette.

97
00:06:06.817 --> 00:06:10.767
The gap between people with and without technology is the digital blank.

98
00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:15.045
A, divide. B, rights. C, space.

99
00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.298
The answer is A: divide.

100
00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.512
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:28.302
What does it mean to be a responsible digital citizen?

102
00:06:37.117 --> 00:06:38.617
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:38.917 --> 00:06:47.920
It means you must be kind online, and you should check facts before you share them. You should also protect your privacy and report bullying.

104
00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.127
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:51.017 --> 00:06:56.931
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and modal verbs (must and should) for online conduct.

106
00:06:57.231 --> 00:07:01.219
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

107
00:07:01.519 --> 00:07:03.788
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

108
00:07:04.088 --> 00:07:06.740
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

